# An inner counter the outer loop does not reset: the store writes 32
# words, 128 B (ptxas unrolls it to 32 stores at param_0 + 0 to 124), the
# outer loop's 8 trips of the inner one's 4, its base 16 B further on
# each outer trip. The outer counter steps by the inner loop's exit, and
# the inner one starts from it: 16·iv_out + 4·iv_in, iv the trip less 1.
# One inner execution touches 16 B of the 512 B its CTA requests.
RUN: %ptxroof analyze %fixtures/micro/carried_counter.ptx | FileCheck --check-prefix=ANN "%s"
ANN: {{^}}$L__BB0_1: // loop: trips 8 | warp * × lane * | exec 256/CTA{{$}}
ANN: {{^}}$L__BB0_2: // loop: trips 4 | global per CTA: requested 512 B, unique 16 B, sectors 128 B | warp * × lane * | exec 1,024/CTA{{$}}
ANN: {{^}}	st.global.u32 	[%rd3], %r1; // global store [16·iv[$L__BB0_1] + 4·iv[$L__BB0_2] + param_0] sectors/req 1 (ideal 1){{$}}
